From 4ecf0ba5a8a100c3259742679d132565b5e6ed99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:52:51 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 43/56] The liveness screen in the shared visual design (task
 16)

Visual only: the controller, its states, the events, the texts and the message keys are unchanged. The layout
follows docs/ui-liveness-spec.md section 9, the same as the Desktop client's:
- Top to bottom: the camera card, the status card, the hint line, the progress row, the tips (failure only), and
  the buttons pinned to the bottom. The content is centred, at most 560 dp wide, and only the tips can scroll.
  Before, the failure state scrolled the whole page and the buttons were out of view.
- Camera card: 3:4, radius 16. At most 45% of the screen height; it takes what is left, so it shrinks when the tips
  need the room. A 40% scrim outside the oval, and a 4 dp oval.
- State badge: 28 dp, on the oval's top centre and inside the card. It was 44 dp and could be clipped.
- Status card: 20 sp semibold, centred, the state colour at 10%, a 1 dp border, radius 12, minimum height 80. A long
  status steps down towards 16 sp where 20 would need a third line. It was 26 sp bold, 3 lines on a 360 dp phone.
- Hint line: 15 sp grey-700, centred. It also holds the recovery text of a final failure. It keeps its place while
  guidance can still arrive.
- Progress row: "Step i of n", a segmented bar (done steps full, the current one at least half), "Attempt a of m".
  After a failed attempt only "n attempt(s) left"; before, it showed both. No bar outside challenges.
- Tips: a grey card at 14 sp, at most 40% of the content height.
- Buttons: one row, equal widths, 48 dp, radius 12. Retry and Close are filled, Cancel and Open settings outlined.
- Colours: primary #1C43A1 (the app bar's), challenge #E8890C (with a dark icon on it), success #2E7D32, failure
  #D32F2F. lib/ui/liveness/liveness_style.dart holds the tokens.
- A 200 ms cross-fade when the status changes, off with the system's reduce-motion setting. The 500 ms guidance
  debounce is unchanged.

Tests (98 -> 238, all passing):
- liveness_page_layout_test (140): all 23 states at 360x640 and 412x915 dp, in English, in Arabic and at a 1.3 text
  scale, with Roboto loaded. It checks:
  - no overflow, and nothing scrolls but the tips;
  - the buttons are on screen and 48 high;
  - the camera card is 3:4 and keeps its size;
  - the badge is on the oval's top centre;
  - the English status takes at most 2 lines;
  - a failed attempt shows one attempts line;
  - the right-to-left order.
  Plus the 200 ms fade and the step bar's fill.
- liveness_page_locale_test: finders for the new structure (the status card's icon, the step bar, the tips card).
- liveness_screenshots_test renders docs/images/android, from the fake engine's events and the placeholder. It is
  skipped without LIVENESS_SCREENSHOTS.

